        "Disclosure 414-1 New suppliers that were screened using social criteria 8"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:text "Disclosure 414-1 New suppliers that were screened using social criteria 8"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 414-1 New suppliers that were screened using social criteria\\nThe reporting organization shall report the following information: REQUIREMENTS\\nPercentage of new suppliers that were screened using social criteria. a.\\nGuidance for Disclosure 414-1 Social criteria can include the topics covered in other GRI Topic Standards (e.g., GRI 401: Employment 2016 , GRI 403: Occupational Health and Safety 2018 , GRI 408: Child Labor 2016 , GRI 409: Forced or Compulsory Labor 2016 )."^^xsd:string .

rso:Disclosure_Disclosure_416_1_Assessment_of_the_health_and_safe a rso:Disclosure ;
    rso:belongsToTopic rso:Topic_GRI_416_Customer_Health_and_Safety_2016_3 ;
    rso:originalText "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories 8"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories\\nThe reporting organization shall report the following information: REQUIREMENTS\\nPercentage of significant product and service categories for which health and safety impacts are assessed for improvement. a.\\nGuidance for Disclosure 416-1 This measure helps to identify the existence and range of systematic efforts to address health and safety across the life cycle of a product or service. In reporting the information in Disclosure 416-1, the reporting organization can also describe the criteria used for the assessment."^^xsd:string ;
    rso:pageEnd 3,
        9 ;
    rso:pageStart 3,
        8 ;
    rso:requires rso:Requirement_7767358861881010631 ;
    rso:sectionLabel "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories 8"^^xsd:string ;
    rso:sourceDocument "GRI 416_ Customer Health and Safety 2016.pdf"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:identifier "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safe"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:name "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories 8"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:text "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories 8"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 416-1 Assessment of the health and safety impacts of product and service categories\\nThe reporting organization shall report the following information: REQUIREMENTS\\nPercentage of significant product and service categories for which health and safety impacts are assessed for improvement. a.\\nGuidance for Disclosure 416-1 This measure helps to identify the existence and range of systematic efforts to address health and safety across the life cycle of a product or service. In reporting the information in Disclosure 416-1, the reporting organization can also describe the criteria used for the assessment."^^xsd:string .

rso:Disclosure_Disclosure_417_1_Requirements_for_product_and_serv a rso:Disclosure ;
    rso:belongsToTopic rso:Topic_GRI_417_Marketing_and_Labeling_2016_3 ;
    rso:originalText "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling 8"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling\\nThe reporting organization shall report the following information: REQUIREMENTS\\na.\\nWhether each of the following types of information is required by the organization’s procedures for product and service information and labeling:\\nThe sourcing of components of the product or service; i.\\nContent, particularly with regard to substances that might produce an environmental or social impact; ii.\\nSafe use of the product or service; iii.\\nDisposal of the product and environmental or social impacts; iv.\\nOther (explain). v.\\nPercentage of significant product or service categories covered by and assessed for compliance with such procedures. b.\\nBackground Customers and end users need accessible and adequate information about the positive and negative environmental and social impacts of products and services. This can include information on the safe use of a product or service, the disposal of the product, or the sourcing of its components. Access to this information helps customers to make informed purchasing choices."^^xsd:string ;
    rso:pageEnd 3,
        9 ;
    rso:pageStart 3,
        8 ;
    rso:requires rso:Requirement_733379653467001133 ;
    rso:sectionLabel "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling 8"^^xsd:string ;
    rso:sourceDocument "GRI 417_ Marketing and Labeling 2016.pdf"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:identifier "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and serv"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:name "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling 8"^^xsd:string ;
    schema1:text "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling 8"^^xsd:string,
        "Disclosure 417-1 Requirements for product and service information and labeling\\nThe reporting organization shall report the following information: REQUIREMENTS\\na.\\nWhether each of the following types of information is required by the organization’s procedures for product and service information and labeling:\\nThe sourcing of components of the product or service; i.\\nContent, particularly with regard to substances that might produce an environmental or social impact; ii.\\nSafe use of the product or service; iii.\\nDisposal of the product and environmental or social impacts; iv.\\nOther (explain). v.\\nPercentage of significant product or service categories covered by and assessed for compliance with such procedures. b.\\nBackground Customers and end users need accessible and adequate information about the positive and negative environmental and social impacts of products and services. This can include information on the safe use of a product or service, the disposal of the product, or the sourcing of its components. Access to this information helps customers to make informed purchasing choices."^^xsd:string .

